  "interpretation": {
    "frozen_primary": "Both rules close globally at the D,G prefix on tested finite rings, but for different reasons: Rule 62 DG reconstructs the source exactly, while Rule 110 DG is injective except for a tiny period-4 phase ambiguity. Full-line locality separates them: Rule 62 has an exact radius-3 DG->Q factor; Rule 110 has no radius<=3 factor.",
    "exploratory": "Starting from G rather than D, Rule 110 reaches finite-ring jet closure at R (G,Q,R) at every tested width, whereas Rule 62 requires deeper levels as width grows before stabilizing at A5 for n>=12. Neither finite-ring closure yields a radius<=3 full-line local law in the tested closed prefix.",
    "caution": "The finite-ring jet closures are near-injective and therefore do not establish compression advantages or infinite-line closure."
  },
